.Dd December 21, 2026
.Dt ICOWM-BINDINGS 5
.Os icowm-1.0.1
.Sh NAME
.Nm bindings.json
.Nd keyboard and mouse bindings for IcoWM
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Pa bindings.json
holds every keyboard shortcut and mouse binding.
The file is optional: absent, the defaults given below are used.
.Ss Syntax
A binding is a chain of modifier aliases and one final key or button
name, joined by
.Ql + :
.Bd -literal -offset indent
modifier1+[modifier2+[modifier3+]]KeyName
.Ed
.Pp
Modifier aliases are the symbolic names the
.Ic modifiers
object defines, such as
.Ql modc
or
.Ql mod1 .
Using an alias rather than a literal name is what lets every shortcut be
remapped by editing that one object.
.Pp
A key name is a standard X11 keysym, such as
.Ql Return ,
.Ql Tab ,
.Ql Left ,
.Ql a
or
.Ql F1 .
A button name is
.Ql button1
through
.Ql button5 .
An empty string leaves the action unbound.
.Pp
So
.Ql modc+mod1+Return ,
with the default modifiers, resolves to
.Ql Control+Alt+Return .
.Ss modifiers
Each alias names the real modifier it stands for.
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic modc Pq default Ql Control
.It Ic mods Pq default Ql Shift
.It Ic modl Pq default Ql Caps_Lock
.It Ic mod1 Pq default Ql Alt
.It Ic mod2 Pq default Ql Num_Lock
.It Ic mod3 Pq unbound by default
.It Ic mod4 Pq default Ql Super
.It Ic mod5 Pq default Ql Hyper
.El
.Ss keyboard.launch
Starts the programs
.Xr icowm 5
names under
.Ic programs .
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic terminal Pq Ql modc+mod1+Return
.It Ic launcher Pq Ql modc+mod1+r
.It Ic file-manager Pq Ql modc+mod1+q
.It Ic web-browser Pq Ql modc+mod1+w
.It Ic editor Pq Ql modc+mod1+e
.El
.Ss keyboard.window
Acts on the focused window.
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic close Pq Ql modc+mod1+c
.It Ic kill Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+Escape
.It Ic iconify Pq Ql modc+mod1+i
.It Ic iconify-all Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+i
.It Ic deiconify-all Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+d
.It Ic arrange Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+a
.It Ic hide Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+u
.It Ic maximize Pq Ql modc+mod1+m
.It Ic fullscreen Pq Ql modc+mod1+f
.It Ic shade Pq Ql modc+mod1+s
.It Ic pin Pq Ql modc+mod1+p
.It Ic decorate Pq Ql modc+mod1+d
.It Ic layer Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+y
.It Ic info Pq Ql modc+mod4+mods+i
.El
.Pp
.Ic move.relative
shifts the window by
.Ic windows.move-step
pixels:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic right Pq Ql modc+mod1+l
.It Ic left Pq Ql modc+mod1+h
.It Ic up Pq Ql modc+mod1+k
.It Ic down Pq Ql modc+mod1+j
.El
.Pp
.Ic move.absolute
sends it to one place outright:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic center Pq Ql modc+mod1+g
.It Ic top-left Pq Ql modc+mod1+y
.It Ic top-right Pq Ql modc+mod1+u
.It Ic bottom-left Pq Ql modc+mod1+b
.It Ic bottom-right Pq Ql modc+mod1+n
.El
.Pp
.Ic resize
grows or shrinks one edge by
.Ic windows.resize-step
pixels:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic right Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+l
.It Ic left Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+h
.It Ic up Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+k
.It Ic down Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+j
.El
.Pp
.Ic send-to.desktop
carries the window to the neighbouring desktop and follows it there:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic north Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+Up
.It Ic south Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+Down
.It Ic east Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+Right
.It Ic west Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+Left
.El
.Pp
.Ic send-to.monitor
carries it to the neighbouring monitor instead:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic north Pq Ql modc+mod1+mod4+mods+Up
.It Ic south Pq Ql modc+mod1+mod4+mods+Down
.It Ic east Pq Ql modc+mod1+mod4+mods+Right
.It Ic west Pq Ql modc+mod1+mod4+mods+Left
.El
.Ss keyboard.wm
Acts on the window manager itself.
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic search Pq Ql modc+mod4+mods+s
.It Ic scratchpad Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+F12
.It Ic toggle-strutless-maximization Pq unbound by default
.It Ic redraw Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+r
.It Ic reload Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+c
.It Ic quit Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+x
.It Ic shortcuts Pq Ql modc+mod4+F1
.It Ic fortune Pq Ql modc+mod4+Backspace
.El
.Pp
.Ic menus
opens one of the two menus:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic root Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+m
.It Ic windows Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+w
.El
.Ss keyboard.desktop
Acts on the desktops of the current surface.
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic add Pq Ql modc+mod4+mods+Right
.It Ic remove Pq Ql modc+mod4+mods+Left
.It Ic show Pq Ql modc+mod4+mods+d
.El
.Pp
.Ic go-to
switches straight to one desktop by number, from
.Ic desktop0
at
.Ql modc+mod1+0
through
.Ic desktop9
at
.Ql modc+mod1+9 .
.Ss keyboard.cycle
Moves through desktops and windows in turn.
.Ic desktop
switches the view without carrying anything along:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic north Pq Ql modc+mod1+Up
.It Ic south Pq Ql modc+mod1+Down
.It Ic east Pq Ql modc+mod1+Right
.It Ic west Pq Ql modc+mod1+Left
.El
.Pp
.Ic window
and
.Ic icon
step through what is on the current desktop:
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic window.next Pq Ql mod1+Tab
.It Ic window.prev Pq Ql mod1+mods+Tab
.It Ic icon.next Pq Ql modc+mod1+Tab
.It Ic icon.prev Pq Ql modc+mod1+mods+Tab
.El
.Ss mouse.window
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic move Pq Ql mod1+button1
.It Ic lower Pq Ql mod1+button2
.It Ic resize Pq Ql mod1+button3
.El
.Ss mouse.cycle
Bound to the wheel over the empty desktop.
.Bl -tag -width Ds -compact
.It Ic north Pq Ql mods+button4
.It Ic south Pq Ql mods+button5
.It Ic east Pq Ql button5
.It Ic west Pq Ql button4
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Pa ${XDG_CONFIG_HOME}/icowm/bindings.json
The file this page describes, at the first of the several locations
.Xr icowm 1
looks in.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
Move every shortcut off Control and onto Super, which is what the
aliases exist for:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
    "modifiers": {
        "modc": "Super"
    }
}
.Ed
.Pp
That is the whole file.
Not one binding is named, yet every shortcut written with
.Ic modc ,
which is most of them, now wants Super where it wanted Control.
Spelling the real modifier into each binding instead would have meant
editing all of them.
.Pp
Rebind one action and leave another unbound, on top of the above:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
{
    "modifiers": {
        "modc": "Super"
    },
    "keyboard": {
        "launch": { "terminal": "modc+mods+Return" },
        "wm": { "quit": "" }
    }
}
.Ed
.Pp
Here the terminal wants Super and Shift together, and quitting has no
shortcut at all.
Everything not named keeps its default, with the new
.Ic modc .
